%%textfont Helvetica 10
%%begintext
version 1

Composed in New York, 1785, by Mr. Hoffmaster in honor of the then 
renowned dancer and actor John Durang.  This is a simplified version.

Cyril Stinnett, Cleo Persinger and others played the A part of this
tune with a wholly different melody in A2.

Durang's Hornpipe as it appears in Cole's gives an example of this variation.
%%endtext
