%%textfont Helvetica 10
%%begintext
Palmer's Square, version 4

This version taken from the playing of Paul Prestopino; last chord may be 
played either minor or major, according to preference.  We chose the minor
chord because Paul Morrissett's fingers prefer it that way.  Prestopino  
learned it from David Kaynor at Ashokan (they both play the last chord major),
and David thinks maybe he learned it at a musical event somewhere in Dalarna,
a historical province or landskap in central Sweden.  Idre (pronounced "Idra") is 
a town in northwestern Dalarna.

According to Laurie Hart, there are two well known versions of this tune, one mostly 
major and the other minor, and this is the major one (with that last chord minored anyway).
%%endtext
% Source: sources/harbormist-com/tunes1/abc.zip/abc/schottis_fran_idre.txt.abc

